        "title": "Eigen directions: when a transformation stays on a line",
        "count": "eigen-directions.json · 14 questions · 4 concepts",
        "prompts": [
          "A = [[2, 1], [−1, 3]] and v = (2, 1). Using column vectors, what is Av?",
          "A = [[3, −2], [1, 4]]. Which vector is A(0, 1)?",
          "Which requirement belongs to the definition of a real eigenvector v of a real matrix A?",
          "A nonzero vector satisfies Av = −3v. What happens to it under this one application of A?",
          "For A = [[1, 0], [0, 0]], the nonzero vector v = (0, 2) maps to (0, 0). Which statement is correct?",
          "Suppose Av = 2v and v is nonzero. What can be concluded about w = −4v?",
          "A = [[2, 0], [0, 1]] and v = (1, 1), so Av = (2, 1). Is v an eigenvector?",
          "For A = [[4, 1], [2, 3]], the trace is 7 and determinant is 10. Which equation and pair give its eigenvalues?",
          "For A = [[2, 1], [1, 2]], which pairing of eigenvector and eigenvalue is correct?",
          "A = [[1, 2], [0, 1]] has the repeated eigenvalue 1. What are its real eigenvectors?",
          "A = [[2, 0], [0, 2]]. How many lines through the origin consist of nonzero eigenvectors away from the origin?",
          "A = [[0, −1], [1, 0]] rotates the real plane by 90°. Its characteristic equation is λ² + 1 = 0. What follows?",
          "A = [[1, 1], [1, 0]] and v = (2, 1), so Av = (3, 2). The two arrows may look nearly aligned in a small diagram. Which exact conclusion is justified?",
          "A nonzero v satisfies Av = −2v. If the same matrix acts twice, what is A²v?"
        ],
